{"id": "P0", "version": 2, "type": "purpose", "subject": "purpose", "owner": "AU-owner", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "QAT-Kit: a modular, human-readable protocol for reflective, composable reasoning: prompt tools (StressTest, TruthWeight and others) that an assistant runs, whose inputs, outputs and handoffs are written as contracts that can be checked rather than merely declared", "rationale": "The repo has no README or purpose file. Taken from Toolkits/Project_Instructions.md L5 (the kit's self-description) and qat/scripts/qat.py L4-9 (why the runner exists: contracts the model might not honour, nothing checking one tool's output fits the next tool's input). docs/ holds only the 2026-11-04 drift inventory and implementation comparison, which describe copies, not purpose. Provisional until Zach states the purpose in his own words; written by kai#telosmith-adoption under DEC-091 (relay-kit-private ledger)", "relations": [{"rel": "supersedes", "to": "P0@1"}], "anchors": [{"path": "Toolkits/Project_Instructions.md", "locator": "L5", "for": "text", "sha256": "e54e761725169203e53dd11112a9095604a3f1dabbe33aa7396472177e2e6824"}, {"path": "qat/scripts/qat.py", "locator": "L4-9", "for": "text", "sha256": "2e89f20b135649b15cb5df398b3098878c5405a1aa71ae5fd33f93d50f376dc2"}]}
{"id": "QAT-R-spec", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Every QAT tool spec (qat/tools/*.qat.md) validates against the spec schema, declares the modules its body uses, and every tool output can be audited against its declared output contract with typed errors (SPEC_INVALID, UNKNOWN_MODULE, MISSING_INPUT, CONTRACT_VIOLATION, TYPE_MISMATCH, UNKNOWN_FIELD)", "rationale": "qat/scripts/qat.py docstring L11-31; the runner never runs a tool, the model does", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:qat.scripts.qat.validate_spec"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:qat.scripts.qat.audit_output"}], "anchors": [{"path": "qat/scripts/qat.py", "locator": "L11-31", "for": "text", "sha256": "2e89f20b135649b15cb5df398b3098878c5405a1aa71ae5fd33f93d50f376dc2"}]}
{"id": "QAT-R-handoff", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "A declared handoff from one QAT tool to another resolves: the target tool and every mapped field exist and the types coerce; an audited output can be mapped onto the next tool's inputs (BROKEN_HANDOFF otherwise)", "rationale": "qat/scripts/qat.py commands index and handoff (L12, L15)", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:qat.scripts.qat.check_handoff"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:qat.scripts.qat.build_handoff"}], "anchors": [{"path": "qat/scripts/qat.py", "locator": "L12-15", "for": "text", "sha256": "2e89f20b135649b15cb5df398b3098878c5405a1aa71ae5fd33f93d50f376dc2"}]}
{"id": "QAT-R-eval", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "text": "Each tool with a spec has eval cases (qat/cases/<tool>.eval.yaml) whose deterministic must_include / must_avoid checks the runner scores against saved outputs (EVAL_FAIL otherwise); judge checks are graded by a model and are not deterministic", "rationale": "qat/scripts/qat.py L16; qat/cases/truth-weight.eval.yaml header; first run in qat/eval-runs/2026-11-04/RESULTS.md", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "QAT-R-spec@1"}, {"rel": "implemented_by", "to": "code:qat.scripts.qat.run_eval"}], "anchors": [{"path": "qat/cases/truth-weight.eval.yaml", "locator": "L1-3", "for": "text", "sha256": "c38a83ca14fb75c5a42a51a71eb38ab019db3f4e785afff167db80a8b4fa5571"}]}
{"id": "QAT-D-canon", "version": 1, "type": "decision", "subject": "design", "status": "proposed", "text": "Pointer, not a decision made here: no copy of any QAT tool is canonical yet. DEC-048 (with Kate's amendment) and DEC-051 item 2 in the relay-kit-private ledger record that the drift inventory declares no canonical copy; docs/DRIFT_INVENTORY_2026-11-04.md lists what each copy contains so that a canonical-source recommendation can be made later with evidence. Copying a file into qat/ does not make it canonical (qat/PROVENANCE.md). Records here must not treat qat/tools/*.qat.md as the canonical tool until Zach decides otherwise. Status stays proposed until Zach accepts this record", "rationale": "DEC-091 (relay-kit-private ledger): each adopting repo's records cite the private ledger decisions that govern it", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}], "anchors": [{"path": "docs/DRIFT_INVENTORY_2026-11-04.md", "locator": "q:no copy is declared canonical here.", "for": "text", "sha256": "378007039261aeec9df0b6b58abb455097d777ac4588a9d80bac06976ec4c26b"}, {"path": "qat/PROVENANCE.md", "locator": "q:Copying a file here does not make it canonical.", "for": "text", "sha256": "4cd52131083a06468b85ec23c66c250dc4a54f11a0b76bfdc075c84dc5065fd4"}]}
